Intuition

Since the array is sorted, we can use Binary Search to efficiently find the first index where the element is strictly greater than x.

The idea is:

If nums[mid] > x, then mid can be a potential upper bound.
But there may be an even smaller valid index on the left side.
So we store mid as answer and continue searching in the left half.

If nums[mid] <= x, then the upper bound must lie on the right side.

Approach
Initialize:
low = 0
high = n - 1
ans = n (default if no valid index exists)
Perform Binary Search:
Find mid
If nums[mid] > x:
Store mid in ans
Move left to search for smaller valid index
Else:
Move right
Return ans
